usage: wolftrap-neuralscope [-h] [--version]
                            {demo,inspect,compare,local,fetch-model,pretrained-plan,pretrained,replay-pretrained,neuron,attention-plan,attention,replay-attention,verify,replay,api-plan,api-run}
                            ...

WolfTrap NeuralScope experimental neural inspection

positional arguments:
  {demo,inspect,compare,local,fetch-model,pretrained-plan,pretrained,replay-pretrained,neuron,attention-plan,attention,replay-attention,verify,replay,api-plan,api-run}
    demo                run a constructed local transformer experiment; no API
    inspect             read local safetensors structure and numeric
                        statistics
    compare             compare two local weight-file inventories
    local               intervene in supported local GPT-2 weights with
                        predeclared token-ID cases
    fetch-model         explicitly acquire the pinned DistilGPT2 numeric
                        assets
    pretrained-plan     freeze fixed tokenized cases before inference; local
                        assets only
    pretrained          compare with Transformers, then run the fixed study if
                        parity passes
    replay-pretrained   reproduce saved reference, intervention and study
                        arrays offline
    neuron              measure one discovery-selected MLP neuron on the
                        pinned local checkpoint
    attention-plan      freeze the fixed 72-head attention study; no inference
    attention           discover one attention head, freeze it, then test
                        held-out inputs
    replay-attention    recompute all attention traces, selection, and results
    verify              verify closed file inventory without model execution
    replay              rerun the recorded local experiment and compare
                        metrics and tensors
    api-plan            preview a behavioral pilot with zero requests
    api-run             dry run by default; --live explicitly enables billable
                        requests

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
